<%
// Sub-tab bar for Main Admin's Settings area (reached via the gear icon
// - views/partials/portal-nav.ejs's settingsHref, routes/main-admin.js's
// /settings redirect). Roles & Permissions, Admins, Website, and Quick
// Links are real separate pages/routes under the hood (unchanged), not
// panels of one shared template - this is just the tab strip every one
// of them includes at the top of <main> so switching between them still
// reads as one settings area. `activeSettingsTab` local: 'roles' |
// 'admins' | 'website' | 'quicklinks'.
//
// A real request: "make every member a user... take away user settings.
// all members will have accounts." The standalone Users tab (account
// list + role editor) is gone - every member already has an account
// managed from their own profile (routes/main-admin-members.js), and
// membership/account approval already has its own home at Members >
// Approvals (utils/membershipApprovals.js).
%>
<div class="view-tabs">
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'roles' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/roles">Roles &amp; Permissions</a>
  <%# A real request: "co-op admin portal. settings gear, admins tab.
      this tab should be located under the main admin portal settings
      gear as a tab. it should not be on co-op admin portal." Moved from
      Co-op Admin's own Settings (routes/admin.js used to have a
      'leaders' tab there) - unchanged otherwise, still just the Admin
      Positions/Leaders manager (utils/adminPositions.js). %>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'admins' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/admins">Admins</a>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'website' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/website">Website</a>
  <a class="view-tab<%= activeSettingsTab === 'quicklinks' ? ' active' : '' %>" href="/main-admin/quick-links">Quick Links</a>
</div>
